# The read must FAIL: Surelog reports the six ILLEGAL lines in dut.sv -- a
# variable with two continuous assignments, or a continuous and a procedural
# driver (UH0759, twice), an assignment pattern for a scalar bit (UH0761),
# more indices than dimensions in a select (UH0760, twice) and more foreach
# loop variables than dimensions (UH0760).  The exact count pins it to
# those: a variable read by a process, a multiply-driven NET, a pattern for
# a packed vector or an unpacked array, a bit of a memory word and a foreach
# over an array of vectors with two loop variables must stay silent.
logger -expect error "Surelog reported 0 fatal, 0 syntax and 6 other error" 1
read_sv -nonote -noinfo -nowarning dut.sv
